## Why This Is Asked
Tests system design for real-time fraud scoring at scale with privacy constraints, multi-tenant data sharing, and safe rollbacks.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming feature store and time-window features
- Hybrid inference paths: server-side and on-device
- Federated learning with differential privacy
- Drift detection and canary-based rollout strategies
- Model calibration and per-transaction explainability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo scoring sketch
function score(tx, globalModel, localModel){
  const feats = extract(tx)
  const s1 = globalModel.predict(feats)
  const s2 = localModel.predict(feats)
  return calibrate((0.6*s1 + 0.4*s2));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle label latency for online updates?
- What metrics trigger rollback and how would you test rollbacks?

## Why This Is Asked
Production anomaly systems face non-stationarity, sparse labels, and strict latency. This question tests end-to-end design, from data schema to deployment, plus practical techniques like self-supervised pretraining and online adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Self-supervised pretraining for unlabeled streams
- Online adaptation with meta-learning
- Two-tower architecture for heterogeneous features
- Drift detection and safe rollout/rollback
- Latency budgeting and quantization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example gating logic for latency-adaptive routing
function route(payload, limitMs) {
  const t0 = performance.now();
  const score = computeScore(payload);
  const dt = performance.now() - t0;
  if (dt > limitMs) return 'fallback';
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate drift detectors in an AB test?
- What failure modes could cause late anomaly alerts and how to mitigate?
